-- Quantifiers over the neighbor fiber (decision record setHop; spec §5, §9). Split from 013-set-hop; twin of 011-neighbor-quantifiers.bqn. (was s05b-neighbor-quantifiers)
-- Six garden plots in a row, planted alternately: 1 0 1 0 1 0. neighbors' is each plot's fiber of adjacent plots. |/ over the fiber asks: any neighbor planted? #/ over the filtered fiber counts them. Both folds read the statement's pre-state, so crops spread exactly one ring per tick: rows 1 and 3 plant (two planted neighbors each), row 5 with one does not, and the new plants never cascade within the tick.
--! registry ../registries/011-neighbor-quantifiers.reg
--! expect sprouting = 0 1 0 1 0 1
--! expect planted = 1 1 1 1 1 0

Plot & |/ neighbors'.Planted , +Sprouting
Plot & !Planted & #/ (neighbors' & Planted) >= 2 , +Planted
